// One charge (0.5 kg) on the floor of a 0.75 m tunnel through soft rock (sandstone, `r`; limestone breaks the same): it clearly blows a
// crater about 2.5 m each way along the tunnel, through the 1 m floor and 1.5 m up into the roof, and leaves
// the rock 3.5 m off whole. About 80 tiles of rock are broken or thrown.
